THE SUPPLY CHAIN BRIEF - Issue 212 - Wednesday

1. Cheaper inference for everyone
OpenRouter announced volume pricing on DeepSeek-V4 Pro, roughly 30% lower, effective October 1. If your unit economics carry an inference line, this is worth a re-run.

2. MX Manufacturing AI Summit recap
Halberd Manufacturing and Northstar Foods both presented case studies on plant-floor visibility. Neither named their software vendor on stage.

3. EU guidance on production telemetry
The Commission published Q3 guidance for processors of production-line telemetry from EU manufacturers. Applies from next year.

